{
  "where_we_lag": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Länsi-Uusimaa lags nationally in crude life-prolonging treatment (25.2%, 95% CI 22.7–27.9 vs 30.4%) and crude MDT recording (0.2%, 95% CI 0.1–0.7 vs 6.0%).",
      "claim_ids": [
        "cty:life_prolonging:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:life_prolonging",
        "cty:mdt_recorded:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
        "nat:mdt_recorded"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Among patients diagnosed in 2019–2023, the county's crude life-prolonging treatment share is 25.2% (95% CI 22.7–27.9; n=267/1058) compared with 30.4% (4522/14873) nationally, with the 95% confidence interval excluding the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:life_prolonging:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Across overlapping treatment categories, the crude curative share is 31.9% (95% CI 29.1–34.7; n=337/1058) versus 27.0% (4009/14873) nationally, excluding the national value, while crude symptomatic care is 40.1% (95% CI 37.2–43.1; n=424/1058) versus 39.5% (5871/14873), with the 95% confidence interval including the national value.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:curative:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:curative",
          "cty:symptomatic:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:symptomatic"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Multidisciplinary team (MDT) meetings are recorded for a crude 0.2% (95% CI 0.1–0.7; n=2/1058) of county patients versus 6.0% (893/14873) nationally, with the 95% confidence interval excluding the national value, though HILMO captures MDT codes only from direct patient contacts and thus measures recording practice rather than care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "bs:coverage:MDT",
          "q:39e6ba43a9"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A crude 28.5% (95% CI 25.9–31.3; n=302/1058) have no treatment record within 12 months versus 27.5% (4089/14873) nationally (95% confidence interval includes the national value); reading this mix of untreated patients and unrecorded care as a data-quality signal, our inference is that the lower crude life-prolonging share (25.2%, 95% CI 22.7–27.9) may partly reflect unrecorded treatment.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "cty:no_treatment_record:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:no_treatment_record",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "how_sure_are_we": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "Public registry tables provide unadjusted 12-month procedure shares, but lack stage adjustment, primary care and referral data, and county-level pathway waiting times.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
        "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
        "bs:coverage:Referral",
        "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "County treatment shares in the public report are crude (not adjusted for age or stage) because stage at diagnosis is missing for ~48% of new patients nationally, and age-adjusted figures digitised from Kuva 16 (precision ±0.5 percentage points) provide national reference lines here only for curative treatment (26.7% for men; 26.9% for women).",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Diagnosis",
          "q:7885b0974f",
          "k16:curative:men:national",
          "k16:curative:women:national"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "A journal article indicates that HILMO hospital discharge diagnoses match the Cancer Registry for about 90% of most cancer types, but this concerns diagnosis concordance only and says nothing about treatment, referral, or MDT recording, which the national lung cancer programme notes is currently incomplete.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "lit:hilmo_90",
          "q:950a2f797b"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Public report data do not measure symptom onset or referrals, do not include outpatient primary care visits or mention occupational health, capture imaging only indirectly as the diagnostic basis in approximately 20% of cases, and show whether a specialist visit (93.6%) or treatment occurred within 12 months without start dates.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "bs:coverage:Symptoms",
          "bs:coverage:Referral",
          "bs:coverage:Primary_care_occupational_health",
          "q:323de0d90d",
          "bs:coverage:Imaging",
          "q:5eb155decc",
          "bs:coverage:First_specialist_visit",
          "bs:coverage:Treatment_start"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "For pathway delays, only preliminary, unpublished national averages from an Yle MOT study are available: 155 days from symptoms to treatment in Finland (compared with 107 in Sweden and 67 in Denmark), comprising 56 days of patient delay, 41 days in primary care, and 58 days in specialist care.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "mot:total_fi",
          "mot:total_se",
          "mot:total_dk",
          "mot:patient",
          "mot:primary",
          "mot:specialist"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "what_to_do_first": {
    "headline": {
      "text": "The team recommends auditing recording completeness for MDT, stage, and drug treatments, reporting access times using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 guidance definitions, and standardising referrals and diagnostic coordination.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "rec:1",
        "rec:2",
        "rec:3",
        "thl:21_2016",
        "q:950a2f797b"
      ]
    },
    "details": [
      {
        "text": "Given Länsi-Uusimaa's crude 0.2% (95% CI 0.1–0.7) MDT recording versus 6.0% nationally and crude 25.2% (95% CI 22.7–27.9) life-prolonging share versus 30.4%, the team recommends publishing county recording completeness for stage, drug treatment, and MDT coding while the roadmap plans uniform coding practices and a national quality registry with 90% coverage.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:3",
          "cty:mdt_recorded:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:mdt_recorded",
          "cty:life_prolonging:Länsi_Uudenmaan_hyvinvointialue",
          "nat:life_prolonging",
          "q:950a2f797b",
          "q:0c7bf2dacb",
          "q:f07a34a300",
          "q:4a856bd695"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Because the Health Care Act sets no maximum time for a cancer suspicion, the team recommends reporting referral-to-treatment access times and handover alerts using THL Ohjaus 21/2016 guidance definitions for 16 cancers, while the roadmap plans target times by 2026–2028 and the Filha diagnostics recommendation is due before the 2030 evaluation.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:1",
          "law:no_max",
          "thl:21_2016",
          "q:24169121a4",
          "q:def306014c",
          "q:8f358a9de6",
          "q:614febebf2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Supported by mentor insight that a weak referral gets a lower urgency rating in specialist care and because local referral instructions vary, the team recommends a standard referral template, referring persistent symptoms after a normal X-ray to a pulmonologist, and naming a diagnostic contact, while the roadmap plans standardised referral criteria and care-coordinator guidance by 2026–2028.",
        "claim_ids": [
          "rec:2",
          "mentor:kaisa_referral",
          "q:556431a0c2",
          "q:82b59905ad",
          "q:c61439b30f",
          "q:abcbb06ae3"
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
